# L018 (2025): stock Android 11 of 2025-05-14 (Projector05141211), the maintainer's own unit. The HY310's
# DRAM words, panel (project 0x30) and display firmware (README.md). Verified 26.10.2026: the image
# h713-l018-v0.97-test3-media-desktop-TEST from main installed on that unit and accepted (doku/222); headphones
# and HDCP 2.2 not tested. *Superseded (26.10.2026):* "nothing of ours has run on it yet. Below verified: TEST
# images for its owner only, never a release image".
BOARD_ID=l018
STATUS=verified
VERIFIED_BY="well0nez, L018 (Projector05141211), v0.97-test3, 26.10.2026"
PROFILE=l018
IMAGE_NAME=h713-l018
# kernel patch 0331: sun50i-h713-hy310.dts plus what the board's stock tree and its pin state under stock
# say differently - no focus motor (PH4/PH5 are twi2 here), no twi1, fan tacho PH13 and the fan's PWM0
# pin PH17 held high, the lamp's pwm-backlight on PWM2/PB4 at the stock duties (it dims as the duty rises), vendor ARISC
KERNEL_DTB=sun50i-h713-l018
# l018_defconfig: the HY310's base (its DRAM block is this board's boot0 word for word) plus
# CONFIG_H713_BOARD_L018 - the gate holds lamp and fan off (PB5 low, PB4 high), the board comes up at the
# stock std mode (lamp PWM2 50 %, fan PWM0 70 %), and the panel sequence keeps PH9 low and leaves PF6
# alone (U-Boot fork b0795ef3079, measured on the unit 25.10.2026: dark gate, picture the right way round)
UBOOT_BOARD=l018
# Optional hardware (boards/README.md, FEATURES), all measured on the owner's unit 25.10.2026 (doku/220): the camera
# (USB UVC "HYSD-VAF02"), the accelerometer (lsm6dsv on twi2, kernel 0334), the focus motor (motor_ctr, PF0..PF3; its
# end switch is dead on that unit, FOCUS_HOMING below), lamp-modes (kernel 0332). *Superseded (26.10.2026):* "lamp-modes;
# the rest not driven yet".
FEATURES="camera accelerometer focus-motor lamp-modes"
# h713-keystone (boards/README.md, KEYSTONE): the lsm6dsv's IIO name and axes - measured in the stand on
# 25.10.2026: -x reads +1 g, z rises with the lens up, y (the hinge) stays at 0; roll's sign not measured -
# and the throw ratio of the board's own stock camprjspe.ini (1.1501, the HY310's 0.8176). The full L018
# optics and this ratio on the HY310's differ by at most 3 px over +-40 degrees pitch and +-15 roll; at
# 18.6 degrees the owner saw the picture straight from in front of the wall (the HY310's: top too narrow).
KEYSTONE="iio_name=lsm6dsv_accel axis_pitch=+z axis_roll=+y axis_vertical=-x throw_ratio=1.1501"
# h713-tv's volume curve (boards/README.md, VOLUME_CURVE): the board's own stock curve out of its audio_config.ini (1 = -50,
# 50 = -12.5, 100 = +0.5 dB, the DSP ends at 0 dB) instead of the HY310's (100 = -9.5 dB). Hearing test 25.10.2026: the DSP at
# 0 dB "completely ok, does not even sound like the loudest", nothing rattles (arbeit/l018-board-20261024/runde3)
VOLUME_CURVE=vendor
# The focus (boards/README.md, FOCUS_HOMING, FOCUS_STEPS): no reference run at probe - the end switch PB1 is dead on the one
# unit measured (25.10.2026, both stops, every pin); homing would drive into the stop. Back to the driver's default when an
# L018 with a working switch has been measured (the owner, 25.10.2026). One press of a focus key 13 msteps instead of 20: the
# whole travel is about 110 msteps (the HY310's several hundred), and 20 was "much too coarse" (the owner)
FOCUS_HOMING=0
FOCUS_STEPS=13
